// Fetches GoogleTest and pulls in gtest_discover_tests(), so the suites can
// be declared. Written out explicitly, so SmartCMake does not insert them.
//
// Two things deliberately stay out of this function:
//
//   enableTesting() — CMake honours enable_testing() at directory scope only.
//     Inside a function it is accepted and then quietly emits no
//     CTestTestfile.cmake, so every test vanishes with no error. The caller
//     does it. (scmake rejects it here rather than let that happen.)
//
//   the name `enableTesting` — that is a built-in statement, and a function
//     may not shadow one, or calls would reach the built-in instead.
function use_googletest() {
    fetch googletest {
        git: "https://github.com/google/googletest.git"
        tag: "v1.15.2"
        options: { INSTALL_GTEST: false }
    }

    include("GoogleTest")
}
